    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static route 0::0/0 next-hop 2001:db8:4::2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static route 0::0/0 next-hop 2001:db8:4::2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static route 0::0/0 next-hop 2001:db8:4::2\\n##\\n\\nNote: While the exact translation isn't 1:1 between platforms, this Junos command achieves the same functional result as the Cisco configuration by:\\n1. Enabling IPv6 routing (implied by creating an inet6.0 RIB)\\n2. Setting a default IPv6 route via the specified next-hop\\n\\nFor a more direct equivalent to just enabling IPv6 unicast routing (without the static route), you could use:\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\nBut this would only handle neighbor discovery, not routing. The first translation provides the complete functional equivalent of the Cisco configuration's combined effects.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static route 0::0/0 next-hop 2001:db8:4::2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static route 0::0/0 next-hop 2001:db8:4::2\\n##\\n\\nNote: While the exact translation isn't 1:1 between platforms, this Junos command achieves the same functional result as the Cisco configuration by:\\n1. Enabling IPv6 routing (implied by creating an inet6.0 RIB)\\n2. Setting a default IPv6 route via the specified next-hop\\n\\nFor a more direct equivalent to just enabling IPv6 unicast routing (without the static route), you could use:\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\nBut this would only handle neighbor discovery, not routing. The first translation provides the complete functional equivalent of the Cisco configuration's combined effects.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all'}]]": 1,
